$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a solution of 2,3-dichloro-phenylamine (2
g, 12.34 mmol) in DMF (10 mL) at room temperature was added
O-ethylxanthic acid, potassium salt (2.37 g, 14.81 mmol). The reaction
mixture was heated to 150 °C and stirred for 4 h. The reaction mixture
was cooled to room temperature, and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The
crude material was diluted with NH4Cl (saturated), and the precipitate
collected on a filter, washed with water (50 mL x 2), and dried under
vacuum to give product, yield 2.2 g, 10.94 mmol, 89%.
7-Fluorobenzothiazole-2-thiol, yield 89%. white powder, 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
7.0 (t, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.10 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (m, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
