$DATUM 2-(isopropylsulfanyl)benzenecarbaldehyde(2): 2-fluoro-benzaldehyde (2.00
g, 16.1 mmol), potassium carbonate (2.45 g, 17.1 mmol) and 2-propanethiol
(1.35 g, 17.1 mmol) were dissolved in 10.0 mL DMF in a 50 mL
round-bottomed flask under dry nitrogen, topped with a reflux condenser.
The reaction mixture was heated to 50 °C for 48 h. After cooling the
mixture was added to 50 mL of saturated potassium carbonate solution, and
the mixture was extracted with 3x50 mL portions of ether. The extracts
were dried with magnesium sulfate and evaporated. The yellow oil residue
of the crude product was further purified by chromatography on silica gel
using 95:5 petroleum ether (60-80) and dichloromethane as eluent to
afford a yellow oil (2.58 g, 89%). 1H NMR(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.32 (d, J =
6.6 Hz, 6H), 3.40 (septet, J = 6.6 Hz, 1H), 7.35 (m, 1H), 7.51 (d, J =
3.8 Hz, 2H), 7.87 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 10.55 (s, 1H) ppm. 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3): δ 22.9, 38.9, 126.7, 130.2, 132.5, 133.8, 135.9, 140.4,
192.0 ppm.
