$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Nickel-Mediated Intermolecular C−S Cross-coupling of Various Thiols and
Aryl Iodides General Procedure A To a stirred slurry of Zn (130 mg, 2
mmol) and NiCl2 (38 mg, 0.3 mmol) in pyridine (0.5 mL) was added ethyl
crotonate (0.12 mL, 0.9 mmol) or bipyridine (57 mg, 0.36 mmol) at room
temperature. Then the temperature rose to 55 °C and vigorous stirring was
continued for 15 minutes. The resulting Ni(0) complex was cooled to room
temperature, to which the solution of aryl iodide (1 mmol) in pyridine
(0.5 mL) was added quickly. After 2 min, the solution of thiol (1~1.2
mmol) in MeOH (2 mL) was added dropwise over a 15-min period. After 3.5
h, the mixture was filtered with a short plug of silica (elution with 60
mL Et2O) and washed with HCl (1N), water and brine, dried over MgSO4,
filtered and concentrated. The crude product was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel to afford desired thioether. 4-Methoxyphenyl
phenyl sulfide (1a)1 1a was prepared (70% yield) according to General
Procedure A. Colorless oil, yield 88%. Rf =0.54 (petroleum ether/EtOAc =
20 : 1); IR (film): νmax = 3060, 2928, 2837, 1591, 1492, 1440, 1289,
1246, 1175, 1101, 1030, 828, 740, 691 cm−1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
7.41 (dd, J = 6.4, 2.0 Hz, 2H), 7.26−7.11 (m, 5H), 6.90 (dd, J = 6.4, 2.0
Hz, 2H), 3.82 (s, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 159.8, 138.6,
135.3 (2C), 128.9 (2C), 128.2 (2C), 125.8, 124.4, 115.0 (2C), 55.4 ppm;
EI−MS (70 eV): m/z: 216 [M]+, 201, 185, 173, 129.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, dropwise addition of thiol solution stage
3; optimized on solvent, ligand, mode of addition and NiCl2 loading,
in-situ generated catalyst (stage 1), optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Mediated Inter- and Intramolecular C-S Coupling of Thiols and
Thioacetates with Aryl Iodides at Room Temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Xu, Xiao-Bo; Liu, Jian; Zhang, Jian-Jian; Wang, Ya-Wen; Peng, Yu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2013), 15(3), 550-553

