$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 2,3-dichloro-phenylamine (2 g, 12.34 mmol) in DMF (10
mL) at room temperature was added O-ethylxanthic acid, potassium salt
(2.37 g, 14.81 mmol). The reaction mixture was heated to 150 °C and
stirred for 4 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature, and
the solvent was removed in vacuo. The crude material was diluted with
NH4Cl (saturated), and the precipitate collected on a filter, washed with
water (50 mL x 2), and dried under vacuum to give product, yield 2.2 g,
10.94 mmol, 89%. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 7.16 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (m, 2H),
10.0 (s, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, key step
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
