$DATUM copper (I or II) chloride complex
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 108-67-8
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: NaOtBu (48 mg, 0.5 mmol) and Cu(II)-TB-30-B
(30 mg, 2 mol %) were placed in a 10 mL round-bottomed flask. A rubber
septum was fitted and mesitylene (0.5 mL), thiophenol (26 μL, 0.25 mmol)
and iodobenzene (39 μL, 0.375 mmol) were added by syringe. The mixture
was magnetically stirred in a pre-heated oil bath at 140°C for 24 h.
After cooling, n-hexane (0,5 mL) was added, the liquid was passed through
a microfilter syringe and the filtrates were analyzed by GC. hybrid solid
: Cu(II)-DA-30-A, metal (mol %): 2, time (h) : 24. Reactant : Thiol : 3,
Halide : 25, Catalyst (Cu mol%) : C (5), Condition : 72 hours.
1-(4-(phenylthio)phenyl)ethanone. White solid. Product : 26, GC yield :
89(%). Rf (5 % AcOEt in hexane): 0.45. GC/MS (m/z, M+. 228), major peaks
found: 228, 213, 184, 152, 139, 121, 109, 92, 77, 65, 51. IR (ν,cm-1):
3079 (s), 3060 (s), 2999 (s), 2961 (s), 2920 (s), 1845 (s), 1898 (s),
1679 (b), 1589 (m), 1556 (s), 1472 (s), 1436 (m), 1403 (m), 1360 (s),
1304 (s), 1262 (b), 1184 (s), 1112 (m), 1096 (m), 1087 (m), 1064 (m),
1024 (m), 957 (s), 843 (s), 821 (m), 760 (m), 694 (m), 617 (m), 590 (m),
502 (m). 1H NMR (δ, ppm; J, Hz): 7.82 (1H, dd, J= 10.4, 2.6), 7.81 (1H,
dd, J= 6.8, 2.1), 7.52-7.46 (2H, m), 7.44-7.37 (3H, m), 7.22 (1H, dd, J=
10.4, 2.6), 7.21 (1H, dd, J= 6.8, 2.1), 2.55 (3H, s). 13C NMR (δ, ppm):
197.1 (C), 144.9(C), 134.5 (C), 133.9 (2×CH), 132.1 (C), 129.7 (2×CH),
128.9 (2×CH), 128.8 (CH), 127.5 (2×CH), 26.4 (CH3). HRMS (ESI) [M+;
calculated for C14H13SO: 229.0687] found m/z 229.0663.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, Cu(I)-TB-30-A copper catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Organic-Inorganic Hybrid Solids with Copper Complex
Framework and Their Catalytic Activity for the S-Arylation and the
Azide-Alkyne Cycloaddition Reactions
