$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(2R,2'R)-3,3'-[(1,4,6-Trihydroxy-5,8-dioxo-5,8-dihydronaphthalene-2,3-diyl)disulfanyl]bis-(2-acetylaminopropanoic
acid) (IXa). To a solution of 0.138 g (0.50 mmol) of
2-hydroxy-6,7-dichloro-naphthazarin (VIIIa) in 20 ml of water and 20 ml
of CH3CN was added 0.179 g (1.10 mmol) of N-acetyl-L-cysteine and 0.210 g
(1.50 mmol) of K2CO3, and the mixture was stirred at 25°C while
monitoring the reaction progress by TLC in system C. Within 1 h the
initial quinone completely converted into polar substances, Rf 0.43 and
0.15. Within 3 h the compound of Rf 0.43 converted into the polar
substance, Rf 0.15. The reaction mixture was neutralized by adding the
cationite KU-2(H+), worked up as described in the preparation of compound
VIIc. Applying the preparative TLC in system C were isolated the band
corresponding to Rf 0.15, the reaction product was eluted from silica gel
with acetone, the eluate was evaporated in a vacuum, the residue was
dissolved in acetone, and the product was precipitated by adding hexane.
Yield of compound IXa 0.193g. From the mother liquor we separated
additionally 0.050 g of chromatographically homogeneous reaction product.
(2R,2'R)-3,3'-[(1,4,6-Trihydroxy-5,8-dioxo-7-ethyl-5,8-dihydronaphthalene-2,3-diyl)disulfanyl]bis(2-acetylaminopropanoic
acid) (IXc). Yield 0.250 g (89%); dark red needle crystals. Rf 0.16 (B),
mp143-147°C. IR spectrum, cm-1: 3400(OH), 3322(NH), 2971, 2935,
1729(C═O), 1650(C═O), 1615(C═O), 1590, 1538(NH), 1383, 1305, 1218, 1135,
966, 841, 808. 1H NMR spectrum (300 MHz), δ, ppm: 1.05 t (3H, CH2CH3, J
7.4 Hz), 1.79 s (6H, 2COCH3), 2.46 q (2H, CH2CH3, J 7.4 Hz), 3.33 d.d
(1H, H1'A, J1'A,2' 8.8, J1'A,1'B 13.4 Hz), 3.37 d.d (1H, H1''A, J1''A,2''
8.8, J1''A,1''B 13.4 Hz), 3.54 d.d (1H, H1'B, J1'B,2' 4.7, J1'B,1'A 13.4
Hz), 3.65 d.d (1H, H1''B, J1''B,2'' 4.7, J1''B,1''A 13.4 Hz), 4.38 m (2H,
H2',2''), 8.21 d (1H, NH, JNH,2' 8.2 Hz), 8.25 d (1H, NH', JNH',2'' 8.2
Hz), 12.72 br.s (2H, 2COOH), 12.85 s (1H, α-OH), 14.01 s (1H, α-OH). 13C
NMR spectrum (75 MHz), δ, ppm: 12.95, 22.73, 22.83, 26.05, 35.73, 35.96,
52.99, 53.07, 108.57, 109.71, 126.30, 137.87, 143.10, 156.27, 160.04,
160.80, 169.74, 169.83, 172.22 (2), 177.90, 184.44. High resolution mass
spectrum, m/z 579.0705 [M + Na]+. C22H24N2NaO11S2. Calculated 579.0714.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM cationite KU-2(H+) used in stage 2
