$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (2-nitro-phenyl)-phenyl ether (3a)
(2-nitro-phenyl)-(3-methoxylphenyl) sulfide (3i). Following above
procedure, 3-methoxyl benzenethiol (4.20g, 30mmol), KOH (1.68 g, 30mmol)
and 1-chloro-2-nitro-benzene (4.72g, 30mmol) were used. 3i (6.97g) was
obtained as a yellow powder in 89% yield. 1H NMR (300MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.22
(d, J = 8.1, 1H, Ar-H); 7.12-7.43 (m, 5H, Ar-H); 7.02 (d, 1H J = 8.1 Hz,
Ar-H); 6.90 (d, 1H, J = 8.1 Hz, Ar-H ); 3.83 (s, 3H, OCH3).
