$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Intra and
Intermolecular C-S bond formation: An oven-dried flask was charged with
CuI (5 mol %), L5 (10 mol %), dithiocarbamate (1 mmol), iodobenzene (1.1
equiv), K2CO3 (3 equiv), and solvent DMSO (1 mL). The flask was kept in a
pre-heated oil bath at 90 oC. Heating was continued for 4 hrs after which
the reaction mixture was cooled and admixed with water (5 mL). The
product was extracted with ethylacetate (2 x 10 mL), organic layer dried
over anh.Na2SO4, concentrated under reduced pressure, and purified over
column of silica gel (EtOAc: Hexane as eluents) to give product 1a in 86
% isolated yield. The identity and purity of the products were confirmed
by spectroscopic analysis. 2-(Phenylthio)benzo[d]thiazole or
2-Phenylsulfanyl-benzothiazole (1a). Methyl
2-(benzo[d]thiazol-2-ylthio)benzoate or
2-o-Methylbenzoatesulfanylbenzothiazole (1h). Gum; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 3.90 (s, 3H), 7.32–7.49 (m, 5H), 7.75 (d, 1H, J = 8.0 Hz), 7.99
(t, 2H, J = 8.8 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 52.5, 121.2, 122.8,
125.4, 126.4, 127.7, 130.4, 131.1, 131.9, 132.7, 135.5, 136.9, 153.6,
164.6, 166.6.; IR (KBr): 3061, 2949, 1714, 1455, 1426, 1258, 1056, 755
cm-1. Anal. Calcd for C15H11NO2S2 (301.38): C 59.78, H 3.68, N 4.65, S
21.28; found C 59.86, H 3.71, N 4.72, S 21.39.
