$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3,5-Dibromo-2,6-bis(propylthio)aniline (2d).
Crude azo An isomeric mixture of azo derivative 12d (5.0 g, 13.4 mmol)
was dissolved in 95% EtOH (50 mL) with stirring at 70 °C. A solution of
NaOH (1.4 g, 35 mmol) and 1-propanethiol (2.56 g, 34 mmol) in 95% EtOH
(15 mL) was added, and the reaction was stirred overnight at 80 °C. Most
of the EtOH was removed and 6 M HCl (40 mL) was added. The mixture was
poured into water (300 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined
extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and passed through a silica gel plug
(CH2Cl2/hexane, 1:2). The solvent was then removed to give 13d (6.5 g) as
a red-orange oil that was used without purification for the next step. An
analytical sample of 13d was obtained by column chromatography
(CH2Cl2/hexanes, 1:3) 3,5-Dichloro-2,6-bis(propylthio)aniline (2c). Crude
azo compound 13c (7.5 g, 18.8 mmol) was reduced and purified as described
for the preparation of compound 2d to give 5.39 g (89% yield from 12c) of
an off-white solid. mp 36-37 °C; 1H NMR δ 0.98 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 6H), 1.57
(sextet, J = 7.3 Hz, 4H), 2.72 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 4H), 5.74 (br. s, 2H),
6.92 (s, 1H); 13C NMR δ 13.5, 23.1, 36.6, 114.4, 118.5, 141.6, 154.2; IR
(KBr) 3452 and 3343 (N-H) cm-1; EI-MS m/z 313, 311, 309 (M, 8:11:36), 225
(100). Anal. Calcd for C12H17Cl2NS2: C, 46.45; H, 5.52; N, 4.51. Found:
C, 46.65; H, 5.55; N, 4.64.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, intermediate isolated after 2nd stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Azo Group-Assisted Nucleophilic Aromatic Substitutions in Haloarene
Derivatives: Preparation of Substituted 1-Iodo-2,6-bispropylthiobenzenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jason; Manka, T.; McKenzie, Virginia C.; Kaszynski, Piotr
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2004), 69(6), 1967-1971

