$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM This was treated with K2CO3 (5.5 g, 40 mmol),
4-chloro-2-nitrobenzonitrile (3.9 g, 21.3 mmol), copper powder (0.38 g, 6
mmol) and DMF (30 mL). The mixture was stirred under nitrogen for 1 h,
diluted with water (100 mL), and extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x 60
mL). The combined extracts were washed with water (100 mL), dried
(K2CO3), and filtered, and volatiles removed to leave a foam. A portion
(0.5 g) was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel with ethyl
acetate followed by recrystallization from 80% aqueous ethanol to give an
analytical sample of 5 as a yellow powder (0.35 g):
4-(2-Hydroxymethylphenylsulfanyl)-3-nitrobenzonitrile (5). Yellow foam,
yield (6.67 g, 89%). mp 120-126 °C; 1H NMR 8.54 (d, 1H, J = 1.8), 7.74
(dd, 1H, J = 1.3 and 7.7), 7.63 (dt, 1H, J = 1.3 and 7.6), 7.58 (dd, 1H,
J = 1.2 and 7.7), 7.51 (dd, 1H, J = 1.8 and 8.5), 7.47 (dt, 1H, J = 1.5
and 7.7), 6.81 (d, 1H, J = 8.5), 4.77 (s, 2H), 1.94 (br s, 1H). Anal.
(C14H10N2O3S) C, H, N.
