$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM bis(4-methoxyphenyl)sulfide 4-Bromoanisole (3.35 mL, 26.73 mmol, 1.0
equiv), 2-propanol (30 mL), potassium hydroxide (3.47 g, 53.46 mmol, 2.0
equiv), tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(0) (154 mg, 0.134 mmol,
0.005 equiv), (S)-BINAP (166 mg., 0.267 mmol, 0.01 equiv) and
4-methoxybenzenethiol (3.3 mL, 26.73 mmol, 1.0 equiv) were heated under a
nitrogen atmosphere for 22-24 h at 83 °C. After the reaction was
completed it was cooled (<30 °C) and quenched with water (30 mL) which
resulted in a small exotherm (~6 °C) and formation of an oil. The mixture
so formed was allowed to stir for 1 h at 10-15 °C. The slurry was
neutralized using concentrated HCl and extracted with ethyl acetate,
washed with brine and dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered and
concentrated to dryness. Obtained a brown solid9, 5.8 g.
bis(4-methoxyphenyl)sulfide, Yield 88% m/z 246; C14H14O2S requires: C,
68.3; H, 5.73; S, 13.0. Found: C, 68.4; H, 5.79; S, 13.0%; 1H NMR (400
MHz, DMSO- d6) δ 7.31 (d, 4H), 6.87 (d, 4H), 3.82 (s, 6H); IR (cm-1)
νmax; 1592, 1571, 1492, 1285.
