$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Identification of the resting state of the catalyst in the reaction of
4-chlorotoluene with 2-propanethiol catalyzed by a combination of
Pd(OAc)2 and CyPF-tBu. 4-chlorotoluene (13 mg, 0.10 mmol), 1,3,5-trioxane
(internal standard), KOtBu (13 mg, 0.11 mmol) and 1,3,5-trioxane (2.4 mg,
internal standard) were weighed into a vial. A solution of Pd(OAc)2 (2.2
mg, 0.010 mmol) and CyPF-tBu (7.0 mg, 0.013 mmol) in 0.5 mL of toluene-d8
were added. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for 1 min and
2-propanethiol was added (9.8 μL, 0.10 mmol). The mixture was transferred
to an NMR tube with a septum-lined screw-cap. A 1H NMR spectrum was
recorded. The mixture was heated at 100°C. 31P{1H} NMR spectra were
obtained during the course of until full conversion of the starting
material was determined by 1H NMR spectroscopy. The yield of the
thioether was 88%. thioether, yield 88%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
