$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(2R,2'R,2''R)-3,3',3''-[(5,8-Dihydroxy-7-methyl-1,4-dioxo-1,4-dihydronaphthalene-2,3,6-triyl)tri-sulfanyl]tris(2-acetylaminopropanoic
acid) (XIa). To a slurry of 0.077 g (0.25 mmol) of
2,3,6-trichloro-7-methylnaphthazarin (Xa) in 22 ml of CH3CN and 10 ml of
water at vigorous stirring was added 0.163 g (1.00 mmol) of
N-acetyl-L-cysteine (IV) and 0.220 g (1.60 mmol) of K2CO3, and the
mixture was stirred at 25°C while monitoring the reaction progress by TLC
in system C. After 2 min the formation of two new colored compounds, Rf
0.74 and 0.64, was observed. After 20 min new polar colored substance, Rf
0.47, was detected. Within 1.5 h the only product, Rf 0.47, remained in
the reaction mixture. The reaction mixture was worked up as in the
synthesis of compound IXa, and product was isolated by the preparative
TLC. Yield 0.150 g (88%); violet needle crystals. Rf 0.47 (C), mp
200-203°C. IR spectrum, cm-1: 3425(OH), 3360, 3323(NH), 1717(C═O),
1631(C═O), 1605(C═O), 1541(NH), 1420, 1384, 1203, 1119, 910. 1H NMR
spectrum (700 MHz), δ, ppm: 1.77 t (9H, 3COCH3), 2.39 s (3H, CH3), 3.27
d.d (1H, H1'A, J1'A,2' 8.7, J1'A,1'B 13.8 Hz), 3.43 m (2H, H1''A,
H1'''A), 3.56 d.d (1H, H1'B, J1'B,2' 4.8, J1'B,1'A 13.8 Hz), 3.68 m (2H,
H1''B, H1'''B), 4.29 d.d.d (1H, H2', J2',1'A 8.7, J2',1'B 4.8, J2',NH8.2
Hz), 4.45 m (2H, H2'', H2'''), 8.28 m (3H, 3NH), 12.87 br.s (3H, 3COOH),
13.08 s (1H, α-OH), 13.35 s (1H, α-OH). 13C NMR spectrum (176 MHz), δ,
ppm: 13.82, 22.15, 22.51, 22.71, 35.18, 35.81 (2), 51.55, 53.04, 53.07,
110.20, 111.01, 125.65, 128.54, 129.24, 136.55, 161.70, 163.72, 169.64,
169.68, 169.71, 171.96, 172.08, 172.34, 176.75, 176.93. High resolution
mass spectrum, m/z 710.0760 [M + Na]. C26H29N3NaO13S3. Calculated
710.0755.
