$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bis(3-methoxyphenyl) sulfide: CuI (1.72 g, 9.00 mmol), neocuproine (1.87
g, 9.04 mmol), and sodium tert-butoxide (12.9 g, 135 mmol) were placed in
a 1000-mL three-necked round-bottom flask. The flask was then equipped
with a condenser and rubber septum and backfilled with argon. To the
mixture, 3-iodoanisole (12 mL, 100 mmol), 3-methoxybenzenethiol (11 mL,
88 mmol), and dry toluene (300 mL) were added through the septum. The
mixture was heated to reflux for 24 h. The reaction mixture was then
cooled to room temperature and filtered through the Celite to remove any
insoluble residues. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure
and purified by column chromatography (silica gel, diethyl ether only)
and distillation (4 mmHg 174-176 °C). Bis(3-methoxyphenyl) sulfide was
obtained as a clear yellow oil, yield 19.2 g, 78.0 mmol, 88 %. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 3.77 (s, 6H), 6.79 (dd, 2H, 3J = 8.0 Hz, 4J = 2.4
Hz),6.89 (t, 2H, 4J = 2.4 Hz), 6.93 (dt, 2H, 3J = 8.0 Hz, 4J = 0.8 Hz),
7.22 (t, 2H, 3J = 8.0 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
